seal     : The first home video game console had no CPU, no software, and no sound. Ralph Baer's machine drew a few movable white dots with discrete transistor-diode logic, and you taped translucent plastic overlays onto your TV for the 'graphics' and colour. Primitive beyond modern imagining — and the start of everything.
